The upstream repository has no NOTICE file. SyberLabs changed the files on 2026-10-26: the text was rewritten
for the SyberLabs host's GitHits launcher (a per-call command that runs the SyberLabs GitHits API client) instead
of the githits binary, npx or MCP tools; only the search, grep and read commands are described; the example,
list, login, research, resolve, package, diff and upgrade guidance was removed; lookups are limited to a failing
check that implicates a third-party package; queries are pinned to the installed version and an exact symbol or
error text; caps on results and read windows, rules for stopping, rules on the characters a host that checks
commands accepts, and a rule on citing sources were added. The same day the text was shortened to cut its cost
in every request. The upstream text's external-content posture and its search-then-read workflow are kept in
shortened form.

